From: Jeremy Melanson <1080872+zish@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 03:24:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: close the browser at a lock, letting Gecko write what
 it holds

At a lock of the vault the spike locked Gecko's keys and went on. Local
storage writes an origin's first writes 5 seconds later, and an
origin's first write makes its database, whose key cannot be made while
the keys are locked: a lock in those 5 seconds lost them. The logins'
and the cards' keys stayed in memory until the process ended.

encriox closes at a lock instead (W17): the app finishes
its windows, out of the recent apps, and shuts Gecko down while it
still holds the profile's keys, so that what it keeps in memory
reaches the disk sealed; then the process ends, and every key with it.
If Gecko has not ended it in 10 seconds, it is ended anyway. Android
Components' engine throws at a shutdown it did not ask for, so the
runtime's delegate is replaced first.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
